  "body": "Closes #839\nClaim: mac/M1\n\n**Problem.** `ReaderSettingsWatchTests` flaked: the watch delivered a settings change after `stop()`.\n\n**Cause.** A change that resumed the watch task is queued on the main actor. `stop()` cancels the task, but the queued loop body still ran `read()` and `changed()` afterwards.\n\n**Change.** The loop body now returns when its task is cancelled (`guard let self, !Task.isCancelled`). `stop()` and the body both run on the main actor, so `stop()` cancels first and the body sees it. Nothing else changes.\n\n**Tests.**\n- `aChangeQueuedBeforeStopIsNeverDelivered` forces the interleaving: the task is parked, a change is posted, then `stop()` runs with no suspension in between, over 20 iterations.\n- The count is snapshotted once the task is parked, because `didChangeNotification` is process-wide and another test may post.\n- Without the guard it fails on every expectation, on iPhone and iPad.\n- Full suite: iPhone green (1476 tests). iPad green except the known flake #564 (`TopicRowActionsTests.aRemovalInFlightIsNotSentTwice`).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CJ1auuPWv2FeT7Q4Ps\n",
