   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5) — REQUEST CHANGES** — head b14a925a (branch fix/839-reader-settings-watch-race, before the PR)\n\n1. **medium** — `ReaderSettingsWatchTests.swift:73,79`: the new test asserts `changes == 1`, but the suite is not `.serialized` and both tests are `@MainActor`, so they interleave at every `Task.yield()`; `didChangeNotification` is process-wide (the other test's `postChange`, any `UserDefaults` write in the host), so the watch can read a change before the test's own post and line 79 fails. Against #839's own criterion (50 passes under a parallel full-suite run). Fix: `let before = changes` after the parking yields, assert `changes == before` (or `.serialized`).\n2. **none on the production fix**: the `Task {}` inherits main-actor isolation; `read` and `changed` are synchronous after the guard, so `stop()` cannot run in between; an element already resumed before `cancel()` is still delivered and the guard drops it; a restart's old task is also covered; `TopicReaderView` is the only caller.\n3. **nit** — the forced ordering is deterministic on the main executor; the 20 iterations add little.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
