   "body": "**Adversarial review round 2 (Opus 5.5) — APPROVE** — head 77f3703e (round 1: REQUEST CHANGES at b14a925a, test only)\n\nFindings: none. Round-1 finding 1 is resolved: `let before = changes` (`ReaderSettingsWatchTests.swift:75`) runs after the parking yields, with no suspension between it, the post, `stop()` and the second loop, all on the main actor. A foreign notification while parked is counted before the snapshot; one after it only queues the body, which runs after `stop()` and is dropped by the guard. Without the production guard, the element handed to the parked iterator is still returned after `cancel()`, so `read` and `changed()` run and both expectations fail on every iteration (reasoned). Whole branch: one guard at `ReaderSettingsWatch.swift:34` with a why-comment, and the test; no ledger needed.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
